    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0082" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg72"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/583: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornibrook</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-09T11:00:00-06:00">September 9, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. Referring to my telegram No. 59, September 6, 8 p.m., copies of
                    correspondence furnished by Foreign Office evening of September 8 show that
                    Nicaragua and Honduras politely reject Costa Rican offer, <pb facs="0083" n="73"
                        xml:id="pg73"/> former considering as still pending United States 1918
                    [apparent omission]<anchor n="29" xml:id="d71-f1"/> and later feeling that owing
                    to action of friendly governments adjustments already under way. Guatemala had
                    made offer and would welcome collaboration but has had official notice that good
                    offices of the United States already accepted. Salvador confident adjustment
                    would be reached but ready to lend friendly aid in event of failure or in
                    response to indication from Governments concerned that intervention would be
                    welcome.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hornibrook</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d71-f1" n="29" xml:id="d71-f1-content">
                <p>For possible clarification, see fifth paragraph of telegram No. 108, September
                    10, 11 p.m., from the Chargé in Nicaragua, <ref target="#pg74">p. 74</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
